{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/docs/typed-backend.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-05T01:39:26.207891Z","id":"f5bfce99777809ea5144723b515605753a6da0b90f5ca9997fe431e10ad9cf2a","body":{"detail":"Not taken for now: it needs a pinned nightly toolchain and either a third-party extractor (building Charon from source is an unreviewed external build) or Provium's own reimplementation of control-flow reconstruction from the MIR graph, and its output is further from the source (iterators as next() loops, basic blocks), which makes consumer proofs harder to read. The syn front end plus Lean's elaborator re-checking every generated definition, and differential scenarios, are used instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":128},"end":{"line":136},"content_hash":"07e846e35305616f60d34837566342c2e4420db99dd50c846989b062fba5acde"},"summary":"Compiler MIR (Charon LLBC or a rustc_public driver) as the typed backend's front end","supersedes":"6ba04106ad848c3c8cef14daf6cefd02c6bed32857a5831786141e4850ffb677","tags":["revisit:closing the front-end trust gap for CORRECTNESS_PLAN P10/M6, or a construct whose types syn-level inference cannot determine","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"provium/docs/typed-backend.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-05T04:51:42.509448Z","id":"8e9336df33db52d678b0437bef9984fbdacc31161464ca143fefe0f8f09419e8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c689f35","summary":"Fixed: verification now measures differential coverage (provium/src/typed/diffcov.rs) and fails on any translated function the scenario does not execute unless it is listed with a reason; Jarl's scenario was extended to execute all 95 translated functions (1739 of 1850 regions), including Install-free persistence, restore, batches and growth. The saturating_sub example no longer applies: Rust.lean's val_saturating_sub lemma rejects a wrong definition at compile time. Operation-level coverage of Rust.lean is re-recorded as its own concern on diffcov.rs.","supersedes":"7c882afb284025cf1b0e4e8bbf3249722c3af18dd752eec0f9a0e660f2ef3a20","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
